# experiment.json Rules

## Status Lifecycle

`wip` → `shipped` → (publish workflow) → `publishable: true`

- `wip`: generation scripts skip this experiment entirely
- `shipped`: ready for content constellation (publish workflow)
- `publishable`: OUTPUT of the publish workflow, not an input gate

## Required Fields

`title`, `description`, `slug` (kebab-case)

## Enum Values

- **status**: `wip`, `shipped`, `archived`
- **profile**: `r3f-scene`, `r3f-shader`, `scrollytelling`, `interaction`, `dom-effect`, `web-audio`, `blank`
- **complexity**: `beginner`, `intermediate`, `advanced`

## Content Object

Tracks which content formats exist. Pre-commit validator cross-checks these flags against actual files on disk:

- `article` → `article/content.mdx` must exist
- `labNote` → `docs/lab-note.md`
- `architecture` → `docs/architecture.md`
- `snippet` → `docs/snippet.md`
- `social` → `docs/social.md`
- `changelog` → `docs/changelog.md`

## Key Semantics

- `legacy: true` experiments are untouchable (18 pre-V2 experiments)
- `updated`, `inspiration`, `related` are often empty -- populate when known
- Read `.agents/rules/experiments.md` for full isolation rules and decomposition guidance
- Check `profile` field and read `.agents/profiles/<profile>.md` for type-specific guidance
